  "comment": "Mantling slice 1 (docs/design/MANTLING.md section 11, designer answers 11.6; docs/port/MANTLING_SLICE1_REPORT.md). Read by MantleRules::GetConfig (Source/CodexTactics/Public/Characters/MantleRules.h) at game start; FMantleConfig's defaults mirror this file (test CodexTactics.Characters.Mantle.TuningFileMirrorsDefaults). The height classes' nominal / tolerance are NOT here: they come from Content/Data/LevelGen/obstacle_heights.json (the level generator's standard; wall_no_traverse.min_cm = the traversal ceiling). Here: the action per class (destination top / over, enabled, marked_edge_only = only obstacles tagged CodexMantleEdge, handled_by vault = the existing vault takes it), the clip table (retargeted root-motion copies; rise / forward = the copy's measured root track, Saved/Logs/setup_mantle_animation.txt; the four NEEDS_REVIEW clips stay out, designer Q4) and the params. Distances cm, times s. Run-up (designer Q2 = A): a run clip only when he is already running and the face lies inside the run clip's forward-warp window (max_forward_warp); else he stops and the standing clip plays; it starts when the face is no farther than the clip's own run-up (its hand contact's distance in its track, x1.05; B17-3) and the first warp window puts the hands on the lip (a clip whose hands slide over the top: its slowest hand frame at the ledge height, align.slide_speed_cm_s). On a top he crouches (Q3). A knockdown or a hit of at least heavy_hit_damage cancels the climb (Q5): he drops back to the base. links.*: the path links (an order path over an eligible obstacle mantles by itself, only for the operative the player commands in Solo; formation moves never take them).",
